"""Produce the human-readable report after the live run and receipt audit finish."""
import json
from pathlib import Path

from experiments.forecast_only.closed_loop import OUT


def main():
    r=json.loads((OUT/'summary.json').read_text());p=json.loads((OUT/'protocol.json').read_text())
    verification=json.loads((OUT/'verification.json').read_text());assert verification['passed']
    lines=['# Fresh closed-loop Tinker replay: conservative vs original','','Both arms used fresh inference from the earlier high-win-rate run’s final checkpoint on the same 72 historical development matches, with three repeats per arm. Each successive prompt reflected the arm’s executed position; the conservative arm showed its actual quarter-share quantity. No saved model predictions were reused.','','## Results','','Totals below sum 216 game-replays per arm, not 216 independent games. Win rate is positive net P&L among game-replays with a trade. All P&L includes the frozen simulator’s fees, spread and delayed fills.','','| Policy | Traded game-replays | Win rate | Total net P&L | Gross losses | Average loss | Worst loss |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for key,label in [('original','Original, fresh inference'),('original_quarter_size_arithmetic','Original, quarter size (arithmetic)'),('conservative','Conservative, fresh inference')]:
        s=r['summaries'][key]
        lines.append(f"| {label} | {s['traded_cases']} | {s['win_rate_traded']:.1%} | ${s['total_pnl']:.2f} | ${s['gross_losses']:.2f} | ${s['average_loss']:.3f} | ${s['worst_case_pnl']:.3f} |")
    lines+=['','The quarter-size original row scales the fresh original outcomes by 0.25. It is a sizing control, not a third inference arm; it cannot establish how the original model would respond to a quarter-share prompt.','','## Paired uncertainty','','Repeated trajectories are averaged within each game, then 72 games are resampled together across policies for 4,000 bootstrap draws. Shared-team dependence is not modeled.']
    for key,paired in r['paired'].items():
        lo,hi=paired['match_cluster_bootstrap_95']
        lines.append(f"- Conservative minus {key}: {100*paired['mean_pnl_delta_per_game_repeat']:+.2f} cents per game-repeat; 95% interval [{100*lo:+.2f}, {100*hi:+.2f}] cents.")
    lines+=['','## Design and interpretation','','The conservative executor uses 0.25 shares, requires more than 5 cents of probability edge over displayed all-in cost, caps all-in cost at 65 cents per share at both selection and delayed fill, and holds a single accepted purchase to settlement. It ignores advisory model actions. The original arm follows the model’s actions with the original one-share execution rules. This comparison changes entry selection, sizing, exit behavior, and policy awareness in the prompt; it is not a sizing-only ablation.','','The original prompt is unchanged. The conservative prompt explicitly describes the executor and per-share costs, and reports its actual position quantity. Both retain the original complete forecast/action JSON schema and validity rules. No dialogue history was added, matching the original environment’s fresh-state prompt design. Seeds match by game, repeat and decision; temperature is 1 and completions are capped at 256 tokens. Both arms use the original sparse decision schedule, not minute-by-minute streaming.','','The conservative policy’s worst possible loss is 16.25 cents per match under its simulated fill limit. Fractional shares and limit-order fills require market-specific validation before deployment. This is not a portfolio-wide bankroll or simultaneous-exposure simulation. Historical game knowledge, repeated development-set inspection and post-hoc policy design remain limitations. Do not treat these results as a protected generalization test.','','## Cost, holdout and verification','',f"Logged requests: {r['usage']['requests']:,}. Logged input tokens: {r['usage']['input_tokens']:,}; output tokens: {r['usage']['output_tokens']:,}. Full-rate token-cost estimate: **${r['usage']['full_rate_cost_estimate_usd']:.3f}**, below the authorized $5. The maximum-token preflight estimate was ${p['upper_token_cost_estimate_usd']:.3f}; the request reservation ceiling was $2.50. These are token-based estimates, not a provider invoice; cached-prefill discounts are excluded. [Pricing source](https://tinker-docs.thinkingmachines.ai/tinker/models/models_and_pricing/).",'',f"Output validity: original {r['validity']['original']:.1%}; conservative {r['validity']['conservative']:.1%}.",'','The protected holdout remains pending enrollment. No protected predictions, resolutions or scores were created. The ledger head matched before and after the live run.','',f"Eight offline tests passed before the run. The post-run verifier checked {verification['verified_predictions']:,} unique request/response pairs and {verification['verified_game_replays']} complete game-replays: prompt hashes, executed position/quantity feedback, reconstructed P&L, risk limits, code/input hashes and unchanged ledger.",'','## Artifacts','','- `protocol.json`: checkpoint, cohort, policy, sampling seeds, source hashes and budget.','- `requests.jsonl` and `predictions.jsonl`: pre-request receipts and fresh completions with execution decisions.','- `matches.jsonl`: per-arm, per-repeat P&L, costs and replay steps.','- `summary.json`: primary metrics, paired uncertainty and usage.','- `verification.json`: post-run invariant checks.','',f"Checkpoint: `{p['checkpoint']}`.",'','```sh','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m unittest experiments.forecast_only.test_closed_loop experiments.forecast_only.test_risk_policy -v','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.closed_loop','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -u -m experiments.forecast_only.closed_loop --live','.venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.verify_closed_loop','.venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.report_closed_loop','```','','The live runner refuses to overwrite an existing protocol. Do not delete that guard to restart an interrupted paid run without reconciling completed requests. No retraining, commit or push was performed.']
    (OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    print((OUT/'REPORT.md').resolve())

if __name__=='__main__':main()
